   613	title: "Database schemas"
   614	---
   615	
   616	OpenClaw stores control-plane state in the shared state database and agent data in one SQLite database per agent. Schema migrations run forward when a database opens. Older OpenClaw builds refuse databases written by a newer schema.
   617	
   618	Schema-version, integrity, canonical-index, and table-existence checks belong to open/admission and the migration owner after migrations; runtime paths must carry admitted schema facts with the handle, never re-query them, and use fresh `PRAGMA data_version` probes to observe foreign commits on the next unpinned read while preserving active SQLite snapshots. Existing per-call checks are legacy and must be migrated when touched.
   619	
   620	Two mechanisms back that contract. CI runs
   621	`scripts/check-native-state-schema-version.mjs`, which fails the build when the
   622	Swift and TypeScript state-database contracts declare different schema versions.
   623	[`openclaw doctor --fix`](/cli/doctor) owns file-to-SQLite migrations and records a
   624	receipt for each one in the shared `migration_runs` and `migration_sources` tables.
   625	
   626	Execution step receipts are separate from these persisted import receipts.
   627	A step blocked by an earlier refusal includes optional `originatingRefusal`
   628	fields `stepId`, `code`, and `message` naming the first failure. See
   629	[legacy state migration](/cli/doctor/state-migrations) for how to resolve it.
