   499	Cron recovery observes each batch in one shared-state read-worker snapshot. Healthy
   500	live receipts need no writer admission. A missing receipt table uses its existing
   501	writable first-use initializer before observation resumes. Process liveness and
   502	local receipt ownership remain with the host; observation never grants repair
   503	authority.
   504	
   505	Each necessary repair runs in its own shared-state worker transaction, rereading
   506	the exact receipt, job markers, and task history. The host supplies current routing
   507	policy and revalidates database, scheduler, cancellation, and receipt ownership at
   508	transaction and commit admission. It retains the serialized outcome before granting
   509	commit; a matching compact native commit receipt certifies publication even if the
   510	ordinary worker reply is lost. Notification intents carry delivery facts without
   511	execution payloads. The host sends them only after commit and native settlement.
   512	Schedule maintenance and settled alert delivery use that same retained-outcome owner.
   513	Maintenance reads active receipts and updates unowned jobs in the worker, with host
   514	reservations and active-job facts prepared under the transaction and checked again
   515	before commit. Alert results update only the exact run, alert timestamp, and
   516	notification identity while delivery remains unsettled. Committed maintenance rows
   517	and notifications publish once even when the ordinary worker reply is lost.
