   519	Startup, timer recovery, foreign-receipt monitoring, and settlement waiters use this
   520	same owner under the existing partition lock. If a later repair candidate fails or
   521	the generation retires, earlier committed interruptions still publish after reloading,
   522	before new scheduling work. Retired timer batches join reservation cleanup and release only
   523	the execution slots they acquired. Schemas, retention, and update behavior are
   524	unchanged; guarded saves and execution authority checks retain their existing owners.
