   526	Read-only Cron inspection runs its native open, row decoding, and close in a
   527	bounded worker task. Ordinary cold reads and artifact-preserving cold reads keep
   528	all SQLite execution off the caller thread. Artifact preservation uses the
   529	existing snapshot owner. The parent owns staging before dispatch and waits for
   530	the source-copy child and reader worker to exit before retiring the staging token
   531	and removing copied bytes. Missing databases remain absent, legacy layouts
   532	are not migrated, and Doctor retains its existing schema checks and errors.
   533	An already-held exclusive source scope still prepares its private copy on the
   534	host: that native owner cannot delegate its drained source to another isolate.
   535	The host retains that exclusion and snapshot until the reader worker exits.
   536	Failed worker retirement or snapshot removal remains registered with the existing
   537	state lifecycle owner, so canonical cleanup can retry that same resource without
   538	replaying the read or releasing its pins prematurely.
   539	This branch retains synchronous snapshot coordination; it is not an entirely
   540	off-thread path.
