   790	summary: "The external-plugin compatibility policy and the dated per-surface compatibility records"
   791	read_when:
   792	  - You need to know whether a compatibility surface is still supported
   793	  - You are checking the removal condition for a specific retained contract
   794	title: "Compatibility policy and records"
   795	sidebarTitle: "Compatibility records"
   796	---
   797	
   798	The order compatibility work follows, and the per-surface records that say what is retained, why, and on what condition it can be removed. Part of the [Plugin SDK migration](/plugins/sdk-migration) guide.
   799	
   800	## Compatibility policy
   801	
   802	External-plugin compatibility work follows this order:
   803	
   804	1. Add the new contract.
   805	2. Keep the old behavior wired through a compatibility adapter.
   806	3. Emit a diagnostic or warning naming the old path and replacement.
   807	4. Cover both paths in tests.
   808	5. Document the deprecation and migration path.
   809	6. Remove only after the announced migration window, usually in a major
   810	   release.
   811	
   812	### Retained helper contracts
   813	
   814	Discord and llama.cpp retain their declared OpenClaw 2026.9.2 host support.
   815	They use the newer prepared-expiry, DM-policy refinement, and live-catalog outcome
   816	helpers when those exports are available, with plugin-local fallbacks for the
   817	2026.9.2 SDK. The fallbacks preserve Discord's timestamp validation, idle-first
   818	expiry ties, and root/account DM-policy validation through the older SDK
   819	validators, and llama.cpp's ready, authentication-rejected, and unavailable catalog outcomes
   820	with credential-profile attribution. They do not retry or suppress errors from
   821	an available newer helper. Remove these fallbacks only when the declared plugin
   822	API floor no longer includes 2026.9.2; test built plugin imports against that
   823	minimum host before changing unconditional SDK imports.
   824	
   825	Voice Call also retains its declared 2026.9.2 host support. Its realtime upgrade
   826	handler keeps the two HTTP rejection responses local because that SDK has no
   827	`websocket-runtime` subpath. Rejection bytes flush before the socket is destroyed,
   828	and socket errors retain their normal cleanup behavior. Remove this local
   829	transport compatibility code only when the declared plugin API floor excludes
   830	2026.9.2.
   831	
   832	Retained compatibility entrypoints keep their shipped caller names:
   833	`inbound-envelope` uses `resolveStorePath`, `provider-catalog-runtime` exports
   834	`resolvePluginProviders`, and `agent-runtime`'s
   835	`resolveThinkingDefaultWithRuntimeCatalog` accepts `loadModelCatalog`.
   836	
   837	`resolvePluginProviders` remains synchronous and returns the existing provider
   838	array. When it borrows from an owned inspection, the Gateway lifecycle or
   839	executable CLI invocation retains the backing resources until its actual work
   840	and cleanup finish. Finish calls using those providers before the host closes;
   841	keeping the array does not authorize use after host retirement. A released
   842	inspection stays retired, and a new lookup through that inspection is refused.
   843	Callers outside an OpenClaw host retain the standalone process lifetime of this
   844	SDK contract; process exit does not guarantee asynchronous plugin disposal.
   845	
   846	Inspection release relinquishes the inspection's own claim. If an SDK host
   847	still borrows the same source, final disposal belongs to that host. The host
   848	reports later disposal failures during teardown; they cannot retroactively
   849	change an already returned inspection result. Internal provider resolvers do
   850	not acquire this compatibility lifetime.
   851	
   852	`text-chunking` retains positional `CodeRegion` inputs with `start` and `end`
   853	offsets for `isInsideCode`. Regions returned by `findCodeRegions` additionally
   854	include parser-owned `block` metadata; callers supplying their own ranges do not
   855	need to provide it.
   856	
   857	### Gateway worker environment creation
   858	
   859	`GatewayRequestHandlerOptions` from `core` and `gateway-runtime` retains the
   860	worker-environment creation contract shipped in OpenClaw 2026.9.5. When
   861	`context.workerEnvironmentService` is available, its `create` method accepts
   862	positional arguments in this order: `profileId`, `idempotencyKey`, `machineClass?`,
   863	`executionMode?`, `projectPath?`, `signal?`, `os?`, and `runSetupScript?`.
   864	Idempotent retries and caller cancellation keep their existing behavior across
   865	host upgrades. Changing this contract requires an explicitly approved SDK
   866	migration.
   867	
   868	### Harness attempt result migration
   869	
   870	In OpenClaw 2026.8.1, `EmbeddedRunAttemptResult` from
   871	`openclaw/plugin-sdk/agent-harness-runtime` requires the canonical `terminal`
   872	field. Source written against the 2026.7 direct alias must migrate when it
   873	constructs results with legacy fields such as `aborted`, `timedOut`, and
   874	`promptError`; retaining the alias name does not make those old constructors
   875	source-compatible.
   876	
   877	Use `AgentHarnessAttemptResult` from the same subpath while migrating a
   878	legacy result producer. That union accepts both the legacy fields and the
   879	canonical result, and the host lifecycle normalizes legacy results before
   880	core consumes them. New producers should construct `terminal`; consumers of
   881	the union must narrow the result before reading it. The current
   882	`EmbeddedRunAttemptResult` contract keeps `terminal` required.
   883	
   884	### Model-provider result compatibility
   885	
   886	`openclaw/plugin-sdk/models-provider-runtime` preserves the `ModelsProviderData`
   887	construction shape and `buildModelsProviderData` return signature published in
   888	`v2026.7.1-2`, including typed adapters that return that shape. These contracts
   889	remain supported until an explicitly approved SDK-breaking boundary.
   890	
   891	Call `buildPreparedModelsProviderData` when forwarding model selections. Its
   892	result includes the required `modelCatalog` with
   893	the selected physical-route metadata. Both builders use one metadata producer;
   894	callers must carry prepared rows forward rather than reconstructing them from IDs.
   895	
   896	Use `getModelsRuntimeChoices(data, provider, model)` from the same SDK subpath
   897	for a selected model. A nonempty array contains that model's eligible runtime
   898	choices. An empty array means the current observation permits no runtime for
   899	that model. `undefined` means the choice is unknown: the model has no observation,
   900	the caller supplied the older result shape, or `data.isCurrent()` reports that
   901	the prepared owner has retired. Do not replace either result with a provider
   902	default or a runtime inferred from its name. Refresh retired data through its
   903	owning catalog before selecting again.
   904	
   905	Omitting `model` returns the provider's browsing union. That union does not
   906	authorize a runtime for every model in the provider. Pass `sessionEntry` to the
   907	builder when browsing for a session so its profile preference, explicit profile
   908	pin, and runtime override participate in the choices. Keep the prepared physical
   909	row and revalidate the selection through the normal command owner; a displayed
   910	choice is not authority to use a retired generation or bypass a session lock.
   911	
   912	Provider plugins can publish native login presence through `prepareSyntheticAuth`
   913	with `nativeAuth: { runtime, mode }`, where `mode` is `api-key`, `oauth`, or
   914	`token`. These facts apply only to the named runtime in the prepared generation.
   915	They do not supply a provider bearer credential or authorize importing one into
   916	an OpenClaw profile. The optional `pluginRoot` context comes from the plugin
   917	loader; use it to resolve the declared dependency from that plugin's installation.
   918	
   919	### Memory read missing results
   920	
   921	Memory managers now return `status: "ok"` for successful excerpts and
   922	`status: "not_found"` when an allowed file is missing. This keeps empty files
   923	and empty ranges distinct from missing files without relying on pagination
   924	metadata.
   925	
   926	At registration, every statusless result from an older external memory manager
   927	preserves its legacy successful-read semantics and becomes `status: "ok"`,
   928	including empty results without range metadata. Only an explicit
   929	`status: "not_found"` reports absence. New producers must emit that status for
   930	missing files; registered-input normalization remains available through the
   931	next Plugin SDK major.
   932	
   933	### Config record migrations
   934	
   935	Use `mergeMissing(canonical, legacy)` from
   936	`openclaw/plugin-sdk/runtime-doctor-migrations` to fill undefined fields without
   937	replacing authored values. It fills existing nested records in place and keeps
   938	authored arrays, nulls, and scalars. Missing values are assigned by reference;
   939	callers own any cloning needed to isolate the migration from its input.
   940	
   941	The helper skips undefined source values and `__proto__`, `prototype`, and
   942	`constructor` keys at each level it merges. It does not recursively sanitize
   943	newly assigned subtrees.
   944	
   945	### Plugin state migration declarations
   946	
   947	Bundled plugins should list every migration under
   948	`doctorContract.stateMigrations` in `openclaw.plugin.json` and export the
   949	matching `stateMigrations` array from their doctor-contract artifact. Keep the
   950	IDs, order, `doctorOnly` flags, and phases identical. Read-only Doctor planning
   951	uses candidate-bundled descriptors to record exact plugin owners without
   952	loading the plugin.
   953	
   954	Installed external plugin artifacts are not part of the copied-state or
   955	candidate content identity. Copied-state planning refuses their migrations,
   956	including manifests that contain descriptor arrays, until candidate validation
   957	binds those artifacts separately. The legacy value `true` continues to locate
   958	their dynamic contract for non-planning Doctor flows.
   959	
   960	Plan-based migrations can use
   961	`definePluginDoctorMigrationFromPlans(...)` from
   962	`openclaw/plugin-sdk/runtime-doctor-migrations` to preserve existing move, copy, preview,
   963	and plugin-state import behavior.
   964	
   965	Migrations may supply a read-only `collectBackupResources` callback, including
   966	through `definePluginDoctorMigrationFromPlans(...)`. Return absolute paths with
   967	kind `sqlite`, `file`, or `directory`, including destinations that do not exist
   968	yet. Never open a writable store or run the migration during inventory. When
   969	`requireLocalResources` is true, reject remote or unlisted data rather than
   970	reporting an incomplete inventory as complete.
   971	
   972	The recovery inventory collector reports one typed
   973	`undeclared-migration-resources` warning per plugin without a callback; its
   974	private state is not included in the recovery set. Malformed declarations and
   975	invalid inventories still fail. Collection does not capture or restore data,
   976	authorize a migration, or replace an updater's required capture checks.
   977	
   978	For single-file imports, `defineLegacyJsonStateMigration(...)` skips missing
   979	sources (`ENOENT`) and values the plugin parser rejects with `null`. Other read
   980	errors and invalid JSON reach Doctor's detection or migration warnings; the
   981	source remains untouched so the operator can fix it and retry.
   982	
   983	Use `phase: "after-session-repair"` when a migration needs canonical session
   984	ownership evidence. Ordinary Doctor detects these migrations; `--fix` applies
   985	them after session repair under SQLite maintenance ownership. The context
   986	provides bounded `readPluginStateEntriesInKeyRange` and
   987	`readSessionIdentityEvidenceBatch` reads, plus
   988	`deletePluginStateEntriesIfUnchanged` only during a fenced repair. Preserve
   989	unknown or ambiguous ownership. Delete only the observed raw rows; callbacks
   990	retained after maintenance ends cannot authorize later writes.
   991	
   992	The setup-entry `legacyStateMigrations` option and feature flag,
   993	`setupFeatures.legacyStateMigrations`,
   994	`BundledChannelLegacyStateMigrationDetector`, and
   995	`ChannelPlugin.lifecycle.detectLegacyStateMigrations` remain supported through
   996	one doctor-pipeline adapter for external plugins, but are deprecated. Removal
   997	plan: remove that adapter after OpenClaw 2027.1 only when a published-plugin
   998	reader sweep finds no remaining users.
   999	
  1000	### AuthStorage SQLite migration
  1001	
  1002	`AuthStorage.forAgent(agentDir)` is the canonical constructor for host session
  1003	storage. It persists provider-default credentials through the agent's
  1004	`openclaw-agent.sqlite` auth-profile rows and never creates `auth.json`.
  1005	Harness plugins receive the prepared storage instance as `params.authStorage`.
  1006	
  1007	`AuthStorage.create(authPath)` remains as a named deprecated adapter for
  1008	existing plugins. The path is used only to derive the owning agent directory;
  1009	the adapter reads and writes SQLite, not the named JSON file. Migrate to
  1010	`forAgent(...)` now. The path-taking form emits
  1011	`AUTH_STORAGE_CREATE_DEPRECATED` and is eligible for removal after
  1012	2026-10-01, provided the published-plugin reader sweep is clean.
  1013	
  1014	`FileAuthStorageBackend` is an internal SQLite-backed adapter, not an exported
  1015	Plugin SDK backend. It is not available as a named import from
  1016	`openclaw/plugin-sdk/agent-sessions`. Harness plugins should use the
  1017	host-prepared `params.authStorage`; host code that constructs storage should
  1018	use `AuthStorage.forAgent(agentDir)`. The internal adapter emits
  1019	`FILE_AUTH_STORAGE_BACKEND_DEPRECATED` and never reads or writes the legacy
  1020	file. Its internal deprecation window does not preserve the former SDK import.
  1021	
  1022	If a manifest field is still accepted, keep using it until docs and
  1023	diagnostics say otherwise. New code should prefer the documented replacement;
  1024	existing plugins should not break during ordinary minor releases.
  1025	
  1026	The dated compatibility registry also tracks shipped annotations that do not
  1027	belong to one legacy subpath. Unless a later date is listed below, these records
  1028	use 2026-10-01 as the earliest review date; removal still requires the reader
  1029	condition in the final column.
  1030	
  1031	| Compatibility code                                | Replacement                                                                                    | Removal condition                                                                                                    |
  1032	| ------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
  1033	| `plugin-sdk-broad-runtime-barrels`                | Focused capability subpaths                                                                    | No bundled or published imports of the seven enumerated broad barrels remain.                                        |
  1034	| `plugin-sdk-provider-owned-helper-shims`          | Provider-local auth/model/replay/OAuth/stream APIs                                             | Every enumerated helper is migrated in official providers and absent from published plugins.                         |
  1035	| `message-presentation-legacy-bridges`             | `MessagePresentation` and channel presentation renderers                                       | Producers and official channel packages no longer emit or read legacy interactive replies.                           |
  1036	| `plugin-sdk-focused-compat-aliases`               | The focused replacement named by each `@deprecated` annotation                                 | Every enumerated alias has zero bundled and published readers.                                                       |
  1037	| `agent-harness-terminal-result-aliases`           | `AgentHarnessAttemptResult.terminal` and `visibleReplies`                                      | Harness plugins no longer read legacy terminal booleans or `sourceVisibleReplies`.                                   |
  1038	| `official-plugin-export-aliases`                  | Canonical Google Meet testing, presentation renderers, and host-owned Discord timeout behavior | Minimum supported official plugin packages no longer import the aliases.                                             |
  1039	| `memory-host-compatibility-aliases`               | Canonical memory tables and prepared runtime config                                            | Memory integrations no longer pass table overrides or call legacy `loadConfig`.                                      |
  1040	| `plugin-runtime-api-compat-aliases`               | Namespaced plugin APIs and focused runtime methods                                             | All enumerated flat API/runtime aliases have no readers.                                                             |
  1041	| `plugin-provider-manifest-compat-aliases`         | Manifest-owned kind/setup metadata and model catalog registration                              | Providers no longer publish runtime kind or legacy catalog hooks.                                                    |
  1042	| `agent-harness-credential-prompt-string-argument` | Options object `{ controlToolsAvailable }`                                                     | Deprecated and warnings start 2026-09-09; supported through 2026-11-30. Remove after that date once callers migrate. |
  1043	
  1044	### Published channel setup compatibility
  1045	
  1046	Slack, Discord, Signal, and Microsoft Teams packages published through
  1047	`2026.7.1` import channel-specific config schemas from
  1048	`openclaw/plugin-sdk/bundled-channel-config-schema`. The published Slack and
  1049	Discord packages also import `createLegacyCompatChannelDmPolicy` and
  1050	`promptLegacyChannelAllowFromForAccount` from
  1051	`openclaw/plugin-sdk/setup-runtime`.
  1052	
  1053	Those exports remain available as deprecated runtime compatibility adapters.
  1054	New and republished plugins should own their config schemas and setup policy
  1055	locally, using generic primitives from `channel-config-schema` and
  1056	`setup-runtime`. The compatibility exports can be removed only after the
  1057	minimum supported published package versions no longer import them.
  1058	
  1059	### Channel setup input field compatibility
  1060	
  1061	`ChannelSetupInput` now keeps only the cross-channel setup envelope typed
  1062	permanently. Channel-specific fields remain typed in a deprecated compatibility
  1063	tier so existing external plugins still compile while plugin authors move those
  1064	fields into plugin-local setup input types.
  1065	
  1066	OpenClaw does not ship major releases. A registry sweep on 2026-07-22 inspected
  1067	426 published out-of-tree channel plugins and removed 21 fields with no readers.
  1068	The 22 retained fields each have a known published reader. Each further field is
  1069	deleted as soon as no published plugin reads it; the retained set shrinks as
