   661	
   662	`channels.<provider>.*` and `tools.elevated.allowFrom.<provider>.*` checkIds are
   663	generated per configured channel/provider, so `<provider>` is a real channel id
   664	(for example `telegram`, `discord`) in actual output, not a literal string.
   665	
   666	The mutable-entry checks use configured `allowFrom` entries, excluding `"*"` and
   667	pairing-store approvals, and report counts and config paths without raw values.
   668	Symbolic `accessGroup:` references are not counted as mutable identifiers.
   669	Mutable aliases are changeable or shared labels; exact, stable identifiers can
   670	instead have unproven ownership. Ingress diagnostics distinguish
   671	`mutable_identifier_disabled` from `identifier_authentication_too_weak`.
   672	
   673	## Related
   674	
   675	- [Security](/gateway/security)
   676	- [Configuration](/gateway/configuration)
