   679	---
   680	summary: "Daily update requests, approximate location, optional anonymous feature statistics, and privacy controls"
   681	title: "Usage telemetry and update checks"
   682	read_when:
   683	  - Checking what OpenClaw sends and what the receiver stores
   684	  - Deciding whether to share anonymous feature statistics
   685	  - Enabling or disabling anonymous feature statistics
   686	  - Disabling all automatic update-check requests
   687	---
   688	
   689	**Automatic update checks send a daily request by default.** It asks whether a
   690	newer version exists and includes the OpenClaw version, operating system, Node.js
   691	version, CPU architecture, and request surface.
   692	Anonymous feature statistics are opt-in.
   693	This page describes update-check telemetry, not requests made by configured
   694	providers, channels, or other services.
   695	
   696	Anonymous feature statistics describe configured channels and providers, plugin
   697	inventory, and a retained session-creation count. They are **off by default**.
   698	When you enable them, they ride along with that same daily update check instead
   699	of adding a second request.
   700	
   701	These reports help inform maintenance priorities. They do not measure individual
   702	plugin invocations, messages, model requests, or active users. Anonymous usage aggregates
   703	are available at
   704	[telemetry.openclaw.ai](https://telemetry.openclaw.ai).
   705	
   706	Declining is a completely normal choice and changes nothing about how OpenClaw
   707	works for you.
   708	
   709	## Inspect what is sent
   710	
   711	Run this command before or after changing your preference:
   712	
   713	```bash
   714	openclaw telemetry show
   715	```
   716	
   717	Add `--json` to get the same state and payload as one machine-readable
   718	document.
   719	
   720	The output shows whether anonymous feature statistics are enabled, why they are
   721	enabled or disabled, the request endpoint, and the last successful check. When
   722	anonymous feature statistics are enabled, it prints a JSON payload preview built
   723	in the CLI process. It does not retrieve a payload from the running Gateway.
   724	When only anonymous feature statistics are disabled, it shows the update-only request
   725	and its `User-Agent` header instead. When automation or update-check policy
   726	disables all requests, it shows `Request: none` with the reason (`request: null`
   727	in JSON).
   728	The preview describes the client request only. It cannot show server-derived
   729	location information.
   730	
   731	## Daily update check
   732	
   733	The default request is:
   734	
   735	```http
   736	GET https://telemetry.openclaw.ai/api/latest-version
   737	User-Agent: openclaw/2026.8.2 (darwin; node/26.0.1; arm64; gateway)
   738	```
   739	
   740	The `User-Agent` contains the OpenClaw version, operating system, Node.js
   741	version, CPU architecture, and whether the request came from the Gateway or
   742	CLI. It has no request body, install identifier, machine identifier, or random
   743	tracking identifier.
   744	
   745	The service responds with the latest version and, optionally, a short
   746	operator-facing note. OpenClaw displays an available update and its note through
   747	the existing update notice. Unreachable services, timeouts, oversized or invalid responses,
   748	and other failed checks do not interrupt startup or normal operation.
   749	
   750	A successful response and its timestamp are cached in the existing shared state
   751	database. Startup reuses the cached result for the next 24 hours, and a running
   752	Gateway checks again during normal maintenance with a small random delay. Failed
   753	checks do not count as successful daily checks.
   754	
   755	For testing or self-hosting, set `OPENCLAW_TELEMETRY_ENDPOINT` to your complete
   756	replacement endpoint URL. The public server source is available at
   757	[openclaw/telemetry](https://github.com/openclaw/telemetry).
   758	
   759	<a id="cloudflare-derived-request-geography" />
   760	
   761	## Approximate location
   762	
   763	Cloudflare provides approximate location: country, region code, city, and timezone.
   764	We store no raw IP addresses or precise coordinates in analytics.
   765	
   766	Recorded update checks include these fields even when anonymous feature statistics
   767	are off or `DO_NOT_TRACK` is set. Missing or invalid fields stay empty.
   768	No additional client payload or prompt is needed.
   769	
   770	Analytics Engine retains records for **three months**. Public aggregates exclude
   771	location information. Disabling requests does not erase existing records.
   772	
   773	This section describes the hosted service at
   774	[telemetry.openclaw.ai](https://telemetry.openclaw.ai). A replacement endpoint
   775	configured with `OPENCLAW_TELEMETRY_ENDPOINT` can use different infrastructure
   776	and processing or storage policies.
   777	
   778	<a id="optional-feature-statistics" />
   779	
   780	## Optional anonymous feature statistics
   781	
   782	Anonymous feature statistics are **off by default**. Interactive setup can offer a one-time
   783	opt-in with **No thanks** selected by default; guided Quick Start skips that
   784	prompt. OpenClaw records a prompt response so setup does not ask again.
   785	Non-interactive and scripted installations do not opt in automatically, but
   786	operators can explicitly enable anonymous feature statistics with `openclaw telemetry on` or
   787	`telemetry.enabled: true`. The enabled setting, not the presence of a prompt
   788	response, controls whether anonymous feature statistics are included.
   789	
   790	When you explicitly enable anonymous feature statistics, the same daily request becomes a
   791	`POST` with a JSON payload in this shape (values are illustrative):
   792	
   793	```json
   794	{
   795	  "schema": 1,
   796	  "version": "2026.8.2",
   797	  "platform": "darwin-arm64",
   798	  "node": "26.0.1",
   799	  "surface": "gateway",
   800	  "features": {
   801	    "channels": ["discord", "telegram"],
   802	    "providerFamilies": ["anthropic", "openai"],
   803	    "plugins": ["codex", "diagnostics-otel"],
   804	    "pluginsEnabled": 9,
   805	    "sessionsLast24h": 14
   806	  }
   807	}
   808	```
   809	
   810	| Field                       | Meaning                                                                                           |
   811	| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
   812	| `schema`                    | Payload format version, currently `1`.                                                            |
   813	| `version`                   | Installed OpenClaw version.                                                                       |
   814	| `platform`                  | Operating system and CPU architecture.                                                            |
   815	| `node`                      | Running Node.js version.                                                                          |
   816	| `surface`                   | Request surface: `gateway` or `cli`; the CLI preview uses `gateway`.                              |
   817	| `features.channels`         | Configured, not explicitly disabled channel IDs backed by public plugins in the inventory.        |
   818	| `features.providerFamilies` | Public provider IDs from configuration, auth profiles, and configured model references.           |
   819	| `features.plugins`          | Public plugin IDs from the enabled inventory, sorted alphabetically.                              |
   820	| `features.pluginsEnabled`   | Total plugins in that inventory, including plugins not named in `features.plugins`.               |
   821	| `features.sessionsLast24h`  | Retained session-creation events timestamped within the preceding 24 hours, not session activity. |
   822	
   823	With an active plugin registry, the inventory includes enabled, loaded plugins
   824	whose code was imported, plus loaded bundle-format plugins. Without that
   825	registry, it falls back to configured manifest enablement. Neither path records
   826	whether a plugin was invoked or a configured channel or provider handled work.
   827	
   828	Named plugins must be bundled, trusted official installs, or match the official
   829	plugin catalog. Private plugin identities are not named. Names are also filtered
   830	and deduplicated, and the service validates them independently. The difference
   831	between `features.pluginsEnabled` and the number of reported names is therefore
   832	not a reliable count of private plugins.
   833	
   834	The session count depends on locally recorded creation events that remain in
   835	the bounded event store. Missing or unreadable state produces zero. It is not
   836	a count of active sessions, messages, or all sessions that existed that day.
   837	
   838	The sender and `openclaw telemetry show` use the same payload builder, but their
   839	plugin registry, configuration, and collection time can differ. The CLI preview
   840	is not a guarantee of the exact next Gateway payload.
   841	
   842	Reports contain no user, account, install, or device identifier. Repeated reports
   843	are not unique installations or users. The service does not maintain a per-install
   844	history or retention measure.
   845	
   846	<a id="what-is-never-collected" />
   847	
   848	### What is not sent or stored
   849	
   850	Neither the update-check `User-Agent` nor the body containing anonymous feature
   851	statistics includes message content, prompts, model names, API keys, credentials, secret references,
   852	file paths, hostnames, account identifiers, user identifiers, or installation
   853	and machine identifiers. OpenClaw does not create a random UUID or other
   854	persistent client identifier for these requests.
   855	
   856	The hosted service's Analytics Engine rows exclude those direct identifiers and raw
   857	client IP addresses, coordinates, postal codes, and physical-device hardware
   858	details. Cloudflare processes connection IP addresses, and the Worker uses them
   859	transiently for rate limiting without storing them in Analytics Engine. Worker
   860	logs are disabled; Cloudflare's separate infrastructure processing is outside
   861	those settings.
   862	
   863	Anonymous feature statistics are separate from optional, operator-configured
   864	[OpenTelemetry export](/gateway/opentelemetry).
   865	
   866	<a id="turn-feature-statistics-on-or-off" />
   867	
   868	## Turn anonymous feature statistics on or off
   869	
   870	Enable or disable anonymous feature statistics at any time:
   871	
   872	```bash
   873	openclaw telemetry on
   874	openclaw telemetry off
   875	```
   876	
   877	You can also configure the same preference directly:
   878	
   879	```json5
   880	{
   881	  telemetry: {
   882	    enabled: false,
   883	  },
   884	}
   885	```
   886	
   887	Set `DO_NOT_TRACK=1` or `DO_NOT_TRACK=true` to force anonymous feature statistics off,
   888	even when `telemetry.enabled` is `true`. `DO_NOT_TRACK` does not disable the
   889	daily update check: OpenClaw sends the update-only `GET` request without a
   890	body containing anonymous feature statistics.
   891	
   892	## Automated environments
   893	
   894	OpenClaw sends nothing when it detects an automated environment, meaning the
   895	`CI` environment variable is set to a truthy value. Continuous integration jobs
   896	are not installations: they would outnumber real operators by orders of
   897	magnitude and make version and platform counts meaningless, and your pipeline
   898	should not report to us on every job.
   899	
   900	This applies to both tiers, so a CI job sends no update check and no anonymous
   901	feature statistics. Setting `OPENCLAW_TELEMETRY_ENDPOINT` overrides the suppression,
   902	because a configured endpoint means the run is deliberately exercising this
   903	path.
   904	
   905	## Disable every automatic update request
   906	
   907	To go fully dark, disable the existing startup update check:
   908	
   909	```json5
   910	{
   911	  update: {
   912	    checkOnStart: false,
   913	  },
   914	}
   915	```
   916	
   917	This stops both tiers and every automatic update request: no update request,
   918	anonymous feature statistics, or update notice, even when `update.auto.enabled` is `true`.
   919	Setting `OPENCLAW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1` also prevents automatic update requests.
   920	Explicit update commands remain available when you choose to run them.
   921	
   922	See [Configuration reference](/gateway/config-observability#telemetry) for
   923	the full `telemetry` configuration and
   924	[Update configuration](/gateway/config-runtime#update) for the
   925	automatic update-check controls.
