   334	summary: "Live CLI backend smoke (Claude, Gemini, other local CLIs) and the APNs HTTP/2 proxy reachability check"
   335	title: "CLI backend and APNs lanes"
   336	read_when:
   337	  - You are validating the gateway against a local CLI backend
   338	  - You are checking APNs reachability through an HTTP CONNECT proxy
   339	---
   340	
   341	## Live: CLI backend smoke (Claude, Gemini, or other local CLIs)
   342	
   343	- Test: `src/gateway/gateway-cli-backend.live.test.ts`
   344	- Goal: validate the Gateway + agent pipeline using a local CLI backend, without touching your default config.
   345	- Backend-specific smoke defaults live with the owning plugin's `cli-backend.ts` definition.
   346	- Enable:
   347	  - `pnpm test:live` (or `OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST=1` if invoking Vitest directly)
   348	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_CLI_BACKEND=1`
   349	- Defaults:
   350	  - Default provider/model: `claude-cli/claude-sonnet-4-6`
   351	  - Command/args/image behavior come from the owning CLI backend plugin metadata.
   352	- Overrides (optional):
   353	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_CLI_BACKEND_MODEL="claude-cli/claude-sonnet-4-6"`
   354	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_CLI_BACKEND_COMMAND="/full/path/to/claude"`
   355	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_CLI_BACKEND_ARGS='["-p","--output-format","json"]'`
   356	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_CLI_BACKEND_IMAGE_PROBE=1` to send a real image attachment (paths are injected into the prompt). Off by default in Docker recipes.
   357	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_CLI_BACKEND_IMAGE_ARG="--image"` to pass image file paths as CLI args instead of prompt injection.
   358	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_CLI_BACKEND_IMAGE_MODE="repeat"` (or `"list"`) to control how image args are passed when `IMAGE_ARG` is set.
   359	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_CLI_BACKEND_RESUME_PROBE=1` to send a second turn and validate resume flow.
   360	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_CLI_BACKEND_CACHE_PROBE=1` to run a fresh Claude CLI turn, a tool-bearing warmup resume, and a no-tool settlement resume before requiring at least 90% prompt-cache reuse on the following dirty-workspace resume. It also verifies that a thinking-level change rotates the live-session generation and that the next steady resume restores at least 90% reuse. This probe disables the image, MCP, and model-switch probes.
   361	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_CLI_BACKEND_MODEL_SWITCH_PROBE=1` to opt into the Claude Sonnet -> Opus same-session continuity probe when the selected model supports a switch target. Off by default, including in Docker recipes.
   362	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_CLI_BACKEND_MCP_PROBE=1` to opt into the MCP/tool loopback probe. Off by default in Docker recipes.
   363	
   364	Example:
   365	
   366	```bash
   367	  OPENCLAW_LIVE_CLI_BACKEND=1 \
   368	  OPENCLAW_LIVE_CLI_BACKEND_MODEL="claude-cli/claude-sonnet-4-6" \
   369	  pnpm test:live src/gateway/gateway-cli-backend.live.test.ts
   370	```
   371	
   372	Cheap Gemini MCP config smoke:
   373	
   374	```bash
   375	OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST=1 \
   376	  pnpm test:live src/agents/cli-runner/bundle-mcp.gemini.live.test.ts
   377	```
   378	
   379	This does not ask Gemini to generate a response. It writes the same system
   380	settings OpenClaw gives Gemini, then runs `gemini --debug mcp list` to prove a
   381	saved `transport: "streamable-http"` server is normalized to Gemini's HTTP MCP
   382	shape and can connect to a local streamable-HTTP MCP server.
   383	
   384	Docker recipe:
   385	
   386	```bash
   387	pnpm test:docker:live-cli-backend
   388	```
   389	
   390	Single-provider Docker recipes:
   391	
   392	```bash
   393	pnpm test:docker:live-cli-backend:claude
   394	pnpm test:docker:live-cli-backend:claude:cache
   395	pnpm test:docker:live-cli-backend:claude-subscription
   396	pnpm test:docker:live-cli-backend:gemini
   397	```
   398	
   399	Notes:
   400	
   401	- The Docker runner lives at `scripts/test-live-cli-backend-docker.sh`.
   402	- `pnpm test:docker:live-cli-backend:claude:cache` requires Anthropic API-key auth. It logs normalized cache usage for every cache-probe resume and requires at least 90% reuse on both the post-settlement dirty-workspace resume and the steady resume after a thinking-level change.
   403	- It runs the live CLI-backend smoke inside the repo Docker image as the non-root `node` user.
   404	- It resolves CLI smoke metadata from the owning plugin, then installs the matching Linux CLI package (`@anthropic-ai/claude-code` or `@google/gemini-cli`) into a cached writable prefix at `OPENCLAW_DOCKER_CLI_TOOLS_DIR` (default: `~/.cache/openclaw/docker-cli-tools`).
   405	- `codex-cli` is no longer a bundled CLI backend; use `openai/*` with the Codex app-server runtime instead (see [Live: Codex app-server harness smoke](/help/testing-live/acp-and-codex#live-codex-app-server-harness-smoke)).
   406	- `pnpm test:docker:live-cli-backend:claude-subscription` requires portable Claude Code subscription OAuth through either `~/.claude/.credentials.json` with `claudeAiOauth.subscriptionType` or `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` from `claude setup-token`. It first proves direct `claude -p` in Docker, then runs two Gateway CLI-backend turns without preserving Anthropic API-key env vars. This subscription lane disables the Claude MCP/tool and image probes by default because it consumes the signed-in subscription's usage limits and Anthropic can change Claude Agent SDK / `claude -p` billing and rate-limit behavior without an OpenClaw release.
   407	- Claude and Gemini support the same probe set (text turn, image classification, MCP `automations` tool call, model-switch continuity) through the flags above, but none of those probes run by default - opt in per flag as needed.
   408	
   409	## Live: APNs HTTP/2 proxy reachability
   410	
   411	- Test: `src/infra/push-apns-http2.live.test.ts`
   412	- Goal: tunnel through a local HTTP CONNECT proxy to Apple's sandbox APNs endpoint, send the APNs HTTP/2 validation request, and assert Apple's real `403 InvalidProviderToken` response comes back through the proxy path.
   413	- Enable:
   414	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST=1 OPENCLAW_LIVE_APNS_REACHABILITY=1 pnpm test:live src/infra/push-apns-http2.live.test.ts`
   415	- Optional timeout:
   416	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_APNS_TIMEOUT_MS=30000`
   417	---
   418	summary: "The OpenAI long-context proof runs, the recommended live recipes, and the curated model matrix"
   419	title: "OpenAI long context and the live model matrix"
   420	read_when:
   421	  - You are crossing the OpenAI long-context pricing boundary on purpose
   422	  - You want the curated modern/small model lists or a copy-ready live recipe
   423	---
   424	
   425	## Live: OpenAI long context
   426	
   427	- Goal: validate exact-model embedded OpenClaw execution through a
   428	  process-owned isolated Gateway, cross the long-context pricing boundary,
   429	  observe a first-class OpenAI Responses compaction item, and prove opaque
   430	  replay plus prefix pruning on the next request.
   431	- Test: `src/gateway/gateway-openai-long-context.live.test.ts`
   432	- Enable: `OPENCLAW_LIVE_OPENAI_LONG_CONTEXT=1`
   433	- Profiles: `OPENCLAW_LIVE_OPENAI_LONG_CONTEXT_PROFILE=full` selects exact
   434	  `openai/gpt-5.6-luna` with a `1050000` total window, `922000` safe active
   435	  input, `128000` maximum output, and `700000` compaction threshold. `reduced`
   436	  reaches the same transport and persistence path with a smaller budget.
   437	- Metrics: `OPENCLAW_LIVE_OPENAI_LONG_CONTEXT_METRICS=1` emits phase timing and
   438	  token observations. These measurements are informational, not pass/fail
   439	  latency targets.
   440	- Long output: `OPENCLAW_LIVE_OPENAI_LONG_CONTEXT_OUTPUT=1` requires a
   441	  deterministic response between 4000 and 8000 output tokens.
   442	- Optional raw read-tool stress:
   443	  `OPENCLAW_LIVE_OPENAI_LONG_CONTEXT_TOOL_OUTPUT=1`. It is not part of the
   444	  default recipe because the effective tool surface may use Code Mode instead
   445	  of exposing the raw read tool.
   446	
   447	Full `922000` input-budget recipe:
   448	
   449	```bash
   450	OPENCLAW_LIVE_OPENAI_LONG_CONTEXT=1 \
   451	  OPENCLAW_LIVE_OPENAI_LONG_CONTEXT_PROFILE=full \
   452	  OPENCLAW_LIVE_OPENAI_LONG_CONTEXT_METRICS=1 \
   453	  OPENCLAW_LIVE_OPENAI_LONG_CONTEXT_OUTPUT=1 \
   454	  node --import tsx scripts/test-live.mts --quiet src/gateway/gateway-openai-long-context.live.test.ts
   455	```
   456	
   457	Reduced-budget recipe:
   458	
   459	```bash
   460	OPENCLAW_LIVE_OPENAI_LONG_CONTEXT=1 \
   461	  OPENCLAW_LIVE_OPENAI_LONG_CONTEXT_PROFILE=reduced \
   462	  OPENCLAW_LIVE_OPENAI_LONG_CONTEXT_METRICS=1 \
   463	  OPENCLAW_LIVE_OPENAI_LONG_CONTEXT_OUTPUT=1 \
   464	  node --import tsx scripts/test-live.mts --quiet src/gateway/gateway-openai-long-context.live.test.ts
   465	```
   466	
   467	### Long-context hard oracles
   468	
   469	The full embedded and native recipes are proof runs, not throughput
   470	benchmarks. They fail unless the following runtime contracts hold:
   471	
   472	- Runtime and model identity are exact: embedded OpenClaw or native Codex as
   473	  requested, both on `openai/gpt-5.6-luna`.
   474	- At least one provider request crosses `272000` input tokens and every call
   475	  reports priority service.
   476	- Embedded OpenClaw receives and persists a first-class encrypted Responses
   477	  `compaction` item, replays the exact opaque item on the next request, and
   478	  prunes the earlier input prefix. The encrypted content must never appear in
   479	  display or diagnostics.
   480	- Native Codex reports an effective window of `875900`, grows beyond the
   481	  `700000` total-scope threshold without a manual compact, and automatically
   482	  compacts on the next turn.
   483	- Each runtime produces a deterministic long response between 4000 and 8000
   484	  output tokens and preserves a durable marker through compaction and a
   485	  Gateway restart.
   486	
   487	Compaction duration, restart latency, turn latency, and total suite duration
   488	are emitted as informational metrics only.
   489	
   490	### Bounded compaction replay
   491	
   492	The bounded replay cases put a verification marker only in synthetic tool
   493	output, reopen the SQLite session, and require the model to recall that marker.
   494	Configure the corresponding provider API key before running either case;
   495	explicit provider failures are test failures.
   496	
   497	Anthropic exercises streamed native compaction and the next request's replay.
   498	Its native threshold has a 50,000-token minimum:
   499	
   500	```bash
   501	OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST=1 ANTHROPIC_LIVE_TEST=1 \
   502	  node scripts/run-vitest.mjs --config test/vitest/vitest.live.config.ts \
   503	  src/agents/anthropic-transport-stream.live.test.ts \
   504	  -t 'replays streamed native compaction from SQLite'
   505	```
   506	
   507	OpenAI exercises automatic client summarization through the managed runner with
   508	a smaller configured context budget, then replays its persisted summary:
   509	
   510	```bash
   511	OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST=1 OPENCLAW_LIVE_OPENAI_COMPACTION=1 \
   512	  node scripts/run-vitest.mjs --config test/vitest/vitest.live.config.ts \
   513	  src/agents/sessions/agent-session.openai-compaction.live.test.ts \
   514	  -t 'automatically compacts tool history and resumes from its SQLite checkpoint'
   515	```
   516	
   517	<Warning>
   518	The full modes deliberately cross OpenAI's long-context pricing boundary and
   519	make several large API calls. Above `272000` input tokens, the whole request is
   520	2× input/cache and 1.5× output; Fast/Priority doubles that tier again. Use full
   521	mode only with explicit spend approval.
   522	</Warning>
   523	
   524	Fresh OpenAI API-key default:
   525	
   526	```bash
   527	OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_OPENAI_API_DEFAULT=1 \
   528	  OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_PROVIDERS=openai \
   529	  OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_THINKING=off \
   530	  pnpm test:live -- src/gateway/gateway-models.profiles.live.test.ts
   531	```
   532	
   533	This proof leaves `OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_MODELS` unset, resolves the model through
   534	the fresh onboarding inference-selection seam, asserts `openai/gpt-6-astra`, and then
   535	runs a real gateway turn with that resolved model.
   536	
   537	GPT-5.6 embedded OpenClaw matrix:
   538	
   539	```bash
   540	OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_THINKING=ultra \
   541	  OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_PROVIDERS=openai \
   542	  OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_MODELS='openai/gpt-5.6-terra,openai/gpt-5.6-luna' \
   543	  pnpm test:live -- src/gateway/gateway-models.profiles.live.test.ts
   544	```
   545	
   546	Docker notes:
   547	
   548	- The Docker runner lives at `scripts/test-live-codex-harness-docker.sh`.
   549	- It passes `OPENAI_API_KEY`, copies Codex CLI auth files when present, installs
   550	  `@openai/codex` into a writable mounted npm
   551	  prefix, stages the source tree, then runs only the Codex-harness live test.
   552	- Docker enables the image, MCP/tool, and Guardian probes by default. Set
   553	  `OPENCLAW_LIVE_CODEX_HARNESS_IMAGE_PROBE=0` or
   554	  `OPENCLAW_LIVE_CODEX_HARNESS_MCP_PROBE=0` or
   555	  `OPENCLAW_LIVE_CODEX_HARNESS_GUARDIAN_PROBE=0` when you need a narrower debug
   556	  run.
   557	- Docker uses the same explicit Codex runtime config, so legacy aliases or OpenClaw
   558	  fallback cannot hide a Codex harness regression.
   559	- Matrix targets run sequentially in one container. The Docker script scales its
   560	  default 35-minute timeout by target count; any outer shell or CI timeout must
   561	  allow the same total. Canonical CI keeps each GPT-5.6 target in a separate shard.
   562	
   563	### Recommended live recipes
   564	
   565	Narrow, explicit allowlists are fastest and least flaky:
   566	
   567	- Single model, direct (no gateway):
   568	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_MODELS="openai/gpt-5.6-luna" pnpm test:live src/agents/models.profiles.live.test.ts`
   569	
   570	- Small-model direct profile:
   571	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_MODELS=small pnpm test:live src/agents/models.profiles.live.test.ts`
   572	
   573	- Small-model gateway profile:
   574	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_MODELS=small pnpm test:live src/gateway/gateway-models.profiles.live.test.ts`
   575	
   576	- Ollama Cloud API smoke:
   577	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST=1 OPENCLAW_LIVE_OLLAMA=1 OPENCLAW_LIVE_OLLAMA_BASE_URL=https://ollama.com OPENCLAW_LIVE_OLLAMA_MODEL=glm-5.1:cloud OPENCLAW_LIVE_OLLAMA_WEB_SEARCH=0 pnpm test:live -- extensions/ollama/ollama.live.test.ts`
   578	
   579	- Single model, gateway smoke:
   580	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_MODELS="openai/gpt-5.6-luna" pnpm test:live src/gateway/gateway-models.profiles.live.test.ts`
   581	
   582	- Tool calling across several providers:
   583	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_MODELS="openai/gpt-5.6-luna,anthropic/claude-opus-4-6,google/gemini-3.5-flash,deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash,zai/glm-5.1,minimax/MiniMax-M3" pnpm test:live src/gateway/gateway-models.profiles.live.test.ts`
   584	
   585	- Z.AI Coding Plan GLM-5.3 direct smoke:
   586	  - `ZAI_CODING_LIVE_TEST=1 pnpm test:live src/agents/zai.live.test.ts`
   587	
   588	- Google focus:
   589	  - Gemini (API key): `OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_MODELS="google/gemini-3.5-flash" pnpm test:live src/gateway/gateway-models.profiles.live.test.ts`
   590	
   591	- Google adaptive thinking smoke (`qa manual` from the private QA CLI - requires `OPENCLAW_ENABLE_PRIVATE_QA_CLI=1` and a source checkout; see [QA overview](/concepts/qa-e2e-automation)):
   592	  - Gemini 3 dynamic default: `OPENCLAW_ENABLE_PRIVATE_QA_CLI=1 pnpm openclaw qa manual --provider-mode live-frontier --model google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview --alt-model google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview --message '/think adaptive Reply exactly: GEMINI_ADAPTIVE_OK' --timeout-ms 180000`
   593	  - Gemini 2.5 dynamic budget: `OPENCLAW_ENABLE_PRIVATE_QA_CLI=1 pnpm openclaw qa manual --provider-mode live-frontier --model google/gemini-2.5-flash --alt-model google/gemini-2.5-flash --message '/think adaptive Reply exactly: GEMINI25_ADAPTIVE_OK' --timeout-ms 180000`
   594	
   595	Notes:
   596	
   597	- `google/...` uses the Gemini API (API key).
   598	- `google-gemini-cli/...` uses the local Gemini CLI on your machine (separate auth + tooling quirks).
   599	- `google-antigravity/...` is not a registered provider or supported setup path. Do not add it to live-test allowlists.
   600	- Gemini API vs Gemini CLI:
   601	  - API: OpenClaw calls Google's hosted Gemini API over HTTP (API key / profile auth); this is what most users mean by "Gemini".
   602	  - CLI: OpenClaw shells out to a local `gemini` binary; it has its own auth and can behave differently (streaming/tool support/version skew).
   603	
   604	## Live: model matrix (what we cover)
   605	
   606	Live is opt-in, so there is no fixed "CI model list." `OPENCLAW_LIVE_MODELS=modern` / `OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_MODELS=modern` (and their `all` alias) run the curated priority list from `HIGH_SIGNAL_LIVE_MODEL_PRIORITY` in `src/agents/test-helpers/live-model-dynamic-candidates.ts`, in this priority order:
   607	
   608	| Provider/model                                      | Notes      |
   609	| --------------------------------------------------- | ---------- |
   610	| `anthropic/claude-opus-5-5`                         |            |
   611	| `anthropic/claude-opus-5`                           |            |
   612	| `anthropic/claude-opus-4-8`                         |            |
   613	| `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5`                         |            |
   614	| `anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6`                       |            |
   615	| `anthropic/claude-opus-4-7`                         |            |
   616	| `google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview`                     | Gemini API |
   617	| `google/gemini-3.5-flash`                           | Gemini API |
   618	| `cohere/command-a-plus-05-2026`                     |            |
   619	| `moonshot/kimi-k3`                                  |            |
   620	| `anthropic/claude-opus-4-6`                         |            |
   621	| `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash`                        |            |
   622	| `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro`                          |            |
   623	| `minimax/MiniMax-M3`                                |            |
   624	| `openai/gpt-5.6`                                    |            |
   625	| `openrouter/openai/gpt-5.2-chat`                    |            |
   626	| `openrouter/minimax/minimax-m2.7`                   |            |
   627	| `opencode-go/glm-5`                                 |            |
   628	| `openrouter/ai21/jamba-large-1.7`                   |            |
   629	| `xai/grok-4.7`                                      |            |
   630	| `xai/grok-4.6`                                      |            |
   631	| `xai/grok-4.5`                                      |            |
   632	| `xai/grok-4.20-0309-reasoning`                      |            |
   633	| `zai/glm-5.1`                                       |            |
   634	| `fireworks/accounts/fireworks/routers/glm-5p2-fast` |            |
   635	| `minimax-portal/minimax-m3`                         |            |
   636	
   637	The curated **small-model** list (`OPENCLAW_LIVE_MODELS=small` / `OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_MODELS=small`), from `SMALL_LIVE_MODEL_PRIORITY`:
   638	
   639	| Provider/model               |
   640	| ---------------------------- |
   641	| `lmstudio/qwen/qwen3.5-9b`   |
   642	| `vllm/qwen/qwen3-8b`         |
   643	| `sglang/qwen/qwen3-8b`       |
   644	| `ollama/gemma3:4b`           |
   645	| `openrouter/qwen/qwen3.5-9b` |
   646	| `openrouter/z-ai/glm-5.1`    |
   647	| `openrouter/z-ai/glm-5`      |
   648	| `zai/glm-5.1`                |
   649	
   650	Notes on the modern list:
   651	
   652	- `codex` and `codex-cli` providers are excluded from the default modern sweep (they cover CLI-backend/ACP behavior, tested separately on [CLI backend and APNs lanes](/help/testing-live/cli-backends) and [ACP bind and Codex app-server lanes](/help/testing-live/acp-and-codex)). `openai/gpt-5.6` itself routes through the Codex app-server harness by default; see [Live: Codex app-server harness smoke](/help/testing-live/acp-and-codex#live-codex-app-server-harness-smoke).
   653	- `fireworks`, `google`, `openrouter`, and `xai` only run their explicitly curated model ids in the modern sweep (no automatic "every model from this provider" expansion).
   654	- Include at least one image-capable model (Claude/Gemini/OpenAI-family vision variants, etc.) in `OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_MODELS` to exercise the image probe.
   655	
   656	Run gateway smoke with tools + image across a hand-picked cross-provider set:
   657	
   658	```bash
   659	OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_MODELS="openai/gpt-5.6-luna,anthropic/claude-opus-4-6,google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview,google/gemini-3.5-flash,deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash,zai/glm-5.1,minimax/MiniMax-M3" pnpm test:live src/gateway/gateway-models.profiles.live.test.ts
   660	```
   661	
   662	Optional additional coverage outside the curated lists (nice to have, pick a "tools"-capable model you have enabled):
   663	
   664	- Mistral: `mistral/...`
   665	- Cerebras: `cerebras/...` (if you have access)
   666	- LM Studio: `lmstudio/...` (local; tool calling depends on API mode)
   667	
   668	### Aggregators / alternate gateways
   669	
   670	If you have keys enabled, you can also test via:
   671	
   672	- OpenRouter: `openrouter/...` (hundreds of models; use `openclaw models scan` to find tool+image capable candidates)
   673	- OpenCode: `opencode/...` for Zen and `opencode-go/...` for Go (auth via `OPENCODE_API_KEY` / `OPENCODE_ZEN_API_KEY`)
   674	
   675	More providers you can include in the live matrix (if you have creds/config):
   676	
   677	- First-party provider plugins: `anthropic`, `cerebras`, `github-copilot`, `google`, `google-gemini-cli`, `google-vertex`, `groq`, `mistral`, `openai`, `openrouter`, `opencode`, `opencode-go`, `xai`, `zai`
   678	- Via `models.providers` (custom endpoints): `minimax` (cloud/API), plus any OpenAI/Anthropic-compatible proxy (LM Studio, vLLM, LiteLLM, etc.)
   679	
   680	<Tip>
   681	Do not hardcode "all models" in docs. The authoritative list is whatever `discoverModels(...)` returns on your machine plus whatever keys are available.
   682	</Tip>
   683	---
   684	summary: "Deepgram, BytePlus, ComfyUI, and the shared image/music/video generation live sweeps"
   685	title: "Media provider live lanes"
   686	read_when:
   687	  - You are running an image, music, or video generation live sweep
   688	  - You changed a media provider plugin and need its live lane
   689	---
   690	
   691	## Deepgram live (audio transcription)
   692	
   693	- Test: `extensions/deepgram/audio.live.test.ts`
   694	- Enable: `DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=... DEEPGRAM_LIVE_TEST=1 pnpm test:live extensions/deepgram/audio.live.test.ts`
   695	
   696	## BytePlus coding plan live
   697	
   698	- Test: `extensions/byteplus/live.test.ts`
   699	- Enable: `BYTEPLUS_API_KEY=... BYTEPLUS_LIVE_TEST=1 pnpm test:live extensions/byteplus/live.test.ts`
   700	- Optional model override: `BYTEPLUS_CODING_MODEL=ark-code-latest`
   701	
   702	## ComfyUI workflow media live
   703	
   704	- Test: `extensions/comfy/comfy.live.test.ts`
   705	- Enable: `OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST=1 COMFY_LIVE_TEST=1 pnpm test:live -- extensions/comfy/comfy.live.test.ts`
   706	- Scope:
   707	  - Exercises the comfy image, video, and `music_generate` paths
   708	  - Skips each capability unless `plugins.entries.comfy.config.<capability>` is configured
   709	  - Useful after changing comfy workflow submission, polling, downloads, or plugin registration
   710	
   711	## Image generation live
   712	
   713	- Test: `test/image-generation.runtime.live.test.ts`
   714	- Command: `pnpm test:live test/image-generation.runtime.live.test.ts`
   715	- Harness: `pnpm test:live:media image`
   716	- Scope:
   717	  - Enumerates every registered image-generation provider plugin
   718	  - Uses already-exported provider env vars before probing
   719	  - Uses live/env API keys ahead of stored auth profiles by default, so stale test keys in SQLite auth stores do not mask real shell credentials
   720	  - Skips providers with no usable auth/profile/model
   721	  - Runs each configured provider through the shared image-generation runtime:
   722	    - `<provider>:generate`
   723	    - `<provider>:edit` when the provider declares edit support
   724	- Current bundled providers covered:
   725	  - `deepinfra`
   726	  - `fal`
   727	  - `google`
   728	  - `minimax`
   729	  - `openai`
   730	  - `openrouter`
   731	  - `vydra`
   732	  - `xai`
   733	- Optional narrowing:
   734	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_IMAGE_GENERATION_PROVIDERS="openai,google,openrouter,xai"`
   735	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_IMAGE_GENERATION_PROVIDERS="deepinfra"`
   736	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_IMAGE_GENERATION_MODELS="openai/gpt-image-2,google/gemini-3.1-flash-image,openrouter/google/gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview,xai/grok-imagine-image"`
   737	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_IMAGE_GENERATION_CASES="google:flash-generate,google:pro-edit,openrouter:generate,xai:default-generate,xai:default-edit"`
   738	- Optional auth behavior:
   739	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_REQUIRE_PROFILE_KEYS=1` to force profile-store auth and ignore env-only overrides
   740	
   741	For the shipped CLI path, add an `infer` smoke after the provider/runtime live
   742	test passes:
   743	
   744	```bash
   745	OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST=1 OPENCLAW_LIVE_INFER_CLI_TEST=1 pnpm test:live -- test/image-generation.infer-cli.live.test.ts
   746	openclaw infer image providers --json
   747	openclaw infer image generate \
   748	  --model google/gemini-3.1-flash-image \
   749	  --prompt "Minimal flat test image: one blue square on a white background, no text." \
   750	  --output ./openclaw-infer-image-smoke.png \
   751	  --json
   752	```
   753	
   754	This covers CLI argument parsing, config/default-agent resolution, bundled
   755	plugin activation, the shared image-generation runtime, and the live provider
   756	request. Plugin dependencies are expected to be present before runtime load.
   757	
   758	## Music generation live
   759	
   760	- Test: `extensions/music-generation-providers.live.test.ts`
   761	- Enable: `OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST=1 pnpm test:live -- extensions/music-generation-providers.live.test.ts`
   762	- Harness: `pnpm test:live:media music`
   763	- Scope:
   764	  - Exercises the shared bundled music-generation provider path
   765	  - Currently covers `fal`, `google`, `minimax`, and `openrouter`
   766	  - Uses already-exported provider env vars before probing
   767	  - Uses live/env API keys ahead of stored auth profiles by default, so stale test keys in SQLite auth stores do not mask real shell credentials
   768	  - Skips providers with no usable auth/profile/model
   769	  - Runs both declared runtime modes when available:
   770	    - `generate` with prompt-only input
   771	    - `edit` when the provider declares `capabilities.edit.enabled`
   772	  - `comfy` has its own separate live file, not this shared sweep
   773	- Optional narrowing:
   774	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_MUSIC_GENERATION_PROVIDERS="google,minimax"`
   775	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_MUSIC_GENERATION_MODELS="google/lyria-3-clip-preview,minimax/music-2.6"`
   776	- Optional auth behavior:
   777	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_REQUIRE_PROFILE_KEYS=1` to force profile-store auth and ignore env-only overrides
   778	
   779	## Video generation live
   780	
   781	- Test: `extensions/video-generation-providers.live.test.ts`
   782	- Enable: `OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST=1 pnpm test:live -- extensions/video-generation-providers.live.test.ts`
   783	- Harness: `pnpm test:live:media video`
   784	- Scope:
   785	  - Exercises the shared bundled video-generation provider path across `alibaba`, `byteplus`, `deepinfra`, `fal`, `google`, `minimax`, `openai`, `openrouter`, `pixverse`, `qwen`, `runway`, `together`, `vydra`, `xai`
   786	  - Defaults to the release-safe smoke path: one text-to-video request per provider, one-second lobster prompt, and a per-provider operation cap from `OPENCLAW_LIVE_VIDEO_GENERATION_TIMEOUT_MS` (`180000` by default)
   787	  - Skips FAL by default because provider-side queue latency can dominate release time; pass `OPENCLAW_LIVE_VIDEO_GENERATION_PROVIDERS="fal"` (or clear the skip list) to run it explicitly
   788	  - Uses already-exported provider env vars before probing
   789	  - Uses live/env API keys ahead of stored auth profiles by default, so stale test keys in SQLite auth stores do not mask real shell credentials
   790	  - Skips providers with no usable auth/profile/model
   791	  - Runs only `generate` by default
   792	  - Set `OPENCLAW_LIVE_VIDEO_GENERATION_FULL_MODES=1` to also run declared transform modes when available:
   793	    - `imageToVideo` when the provider declares `capabilities.imageToVideo.enabled` and the selected provider/model accepts buffer-backed local image input in the shared sweep
   794	    - `videoToVideo` when the provider declares `capabilities.videoToVideo.enabled` and the selected provider/model accepts buffer-backed local video input in the shared sweep
   795	  - Current declared-but-skipped `imageToVideo` provider in the shared sweep:
   796	    - `vydra` (buffer-backed local image input is not supported in this lane)
   797	  - Provider-specific Vydra coverage:
   798	    - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST=1 OPENCLAW_LIVE_VYDRA_VIDEO=1 pnpm test:live -- extensions/vydra/vydra.live.test.ts`
   799	    - That file runs `veo3` text-to-video plus a `kling` image-to-video lane that uses a remote image URL fixture by default (`OPENCLAW_LIVE_VYDRA_KLING_IMAGE_URL` to override).
   800	  - Provider-specific xAI coverage:
   801	    - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST=1 OPENCLAW_LIVE_XAI_VIDEO=1 pnpm test:live -- extensions/xai/xai.live.test.ts -t "classic Grok Imagine"`
   802	    - The classic case generates a square local PNG first frame, omits geometry, requests a one-second image-to-video clip, polls to completion, and verifies the downloaded buffer.
   803	    - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST=1 OPENCLAW_LIVE_XAI_VIDEO=1 pnpm test:live -- extensions/xai/xai.live.test.ts -t "Grok Imagine Video 1.5"`
   804	    - The 1.5 case generates a local PNG first frame, requests a one-second 1080P image-to-video clip, polls to completion, and verifies the downloaded buffer.
   805	  - Current `videoToVideo` live coverage:
   806	    - `runway` only when the selected model resolves to `gen4_aleph`
   807	  - Current declared-but-skipped `videoToVideo` providers in the shared sweep:
   808	    - `alibaba`, `google`, `openai`, `qwen`, `xai` because those paths currently require remote `http(s)` reference URLs rather than buffer-backed local input
   809	- Optional narrowing:
   810	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_VIDEO_GENERATION_PROVIDERS="deepinfra,google,openai,runway"`
   811	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_VIDEO_GENERATION_MODELS="google/veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview,openai/sora-2,runway/gen4_aleph"`
   812	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_VIDEO_GENERATION_SKIP_PROVIDERS=""` to include every provider in the default sweep, including FAL
   813	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_VIDEO_GENERATION_TIMEOUT_MS=60000` to reduce each provider operation cap for an aggressive smoke run
   814	- Optional auth behavior:
   815	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_REQUIRE_PROFILE_KEYS=1` to force profile-store auth and ignore env-only overrides
   816	
   817	## Media live harness
   818	
   819	- Command: `pnpm test:live:media`
   820	- Entrypoint: `test/e2e/qa-lab/media/hosted-media-provider-live.ts`, which runs `pnpm test:live -- <suite-test-file>` per selected suite, so heartbeat and quiet-mode behavior stay consistent with other `pnpm test:live` runs.
   821	- Purpose:
   822	  - Runs the shared image, music, and video live suites through one repo-native entrypoint
   823	  - Auto-loads missing provider env vars from `~/.profile`
   824	  - Auto-narrows each suite to providers that currently have usable auth by default
   825	- Flags:
   826	  - `--providers <csv>` global provider filter; `--image-providers` / `--music-providers` / `--video-providers` scope a filter to one suite
   827	  - `--all-providers` skips the auth-based auto-filter
   828	  - `--allow-empty` exits `0` when filtering leaves no runnable providers
   829	  - `--quiet` / `--no-quiet` passed through to `test:live`
   830	- Examples:
   831	  - `pnpm test:live:media`
   832	  - `pnpm test:live:media image video --providers openai,google,minimax`
   833	  - `pnpm test:live:media video --video-providers openai,runway --all-providers`
   834	  - `pnpm test:live:media music --quiet`
   835	---
   836	summary: "The two-layer live model smoke: direct completion and the gateway + dev agent pipeline"
   837	title: "Live model smoke (profile keys)"
   838	read_when:
   839	  - You are smoking a provider or model with your own profile keys
   840	  - You need to tell a broken provider key apart from a broken gateway pipeline
   841	---
   842	
   843	## Live: model smoke (profile keys)
   844	
   845	Live model tests are split into two layers so failures are isolated:
   846	
   847	- "Direct model" tells you whether the provider/model can answer at all with the given key.
   848	- "Gateway smoke" tells you whether the full gateway+agent pipeline works for that model (sessions, history, tools, sandbox policy, etc.).
   849	
   850	The curated model lists on
   851	[Live: model matrix](/help/testing-live/long-context-and-matrix#live-model-matrix-what-we-cover)
   852	live in `src/agents/test-helpers/live-model-dynamic-candidates.ts` and
   853	change over time; treat the arrays there as the source of truth, not this
   854	page.
   855	
   856	MiniMax M3 uses `minimax/MiniMax-M3` as its default provider/model reference.
   857	
   858	### Layer 1: Direct model completion (no gateway)
   859	
   860	- Test: `src/agents/models.profiles.live.test.ts`
   861	- Goal:
   862	  - Enumerate discovered models
   863	  - Use `getApiKeyForModel` to select models you have creds for
   864	  - Run a small completion per model (and targeted regressions where needed)
   865	- How to enable:
   866	  - `pnpm test:live` (or `OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST=1` if invoking Vitest directly)
   867	  - Set `OPENCLAW_LIVE_MODELS=modern`, `small`, or `all` (alias for `modern`) to actually run this suite; otherwise it skips, so `pnpm test:live` on its own stays focused on gateway smoke.
   868	- How to select models:
   869	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_MODELS=modern` runs the curated high-signal priority list (see [Live: model matrix](/help/testing-live/long-context-and-matrix#live-model-matrix-what-we-cover))
   870	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_MODELS=small` runs the curated small-model priority list
   871	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_MODELS=all` is an alias for `modern`
   872	  - or `OPENCLAW_LIVE_MODELS="openai/gpt-5.6-luna,anthropic/claude-opus-4-6,..."` (comma allowlist)
   873	  - Local Ollama small-model runs default to `http://127.0.0.1:11434`; set `OPENCLAW_LIVE_OLLAMA_BASE_URL` only for LAN, custom, or Ollama Cloud endpoints.
   874	  - Modern/all and small sweeps default to their curated-list length as a cap; set `OPENCLAW_LIVE_MAX_MODELS=0` for an exhaustive selected-profile sweep or a positive number for a smaller cap.
   875	  - Exhaustive sweeps use `OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST_TIMEOUT_MS` for the whole direct-model test timeout. Default: 60 minutes.
   876	  - Direct-model probes run with 20-way parallelism by default; set `OPENCLAW_LIVE_MODEL_CONCURRENCY` to override.
   877	- How to select providers:
   878	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_PROVIDERS="google,google-gemini-cli"` (comma allowlist)
   879	- Where keys come from:
   880	  - By default: profile store and env fallbacks
   881	  - Set `OPENCLAW_LIVE_REQUIRE_PROFILE_KEYS=1` to enforce **profile store** only
   882	- Why this exists:
   883	  - Separates "provider API is broken / key is invalid" from "gateway agent pipeline is broken"
   884	  - Contains small, isolated regressions (example: OpenAI Responses/Codex Responses reasoning replay + tool-call flows)
   885	
   886	### Layer 2: Gateway + dev agent smoke (what "@openclaw" actually does)
   887	
   888	- Test: `src/gateway/gateway-models.profiles.live.test.ts`
   889	- Goal:
   890	  - Spin up an in-process gateway
   891	  - Create/patch an `agent:dev:*` session (model override per run)
   892	  - Iterate models-with-keys and assert:
   893	    - "meaningful" response (no tools)
   894	    - a real tool invocation works (read probe)
   895	    - optional extra tool probes (exec+read probe)
   896	    - OpenAI regression paths (tool-call-only -> follow-up) keep working
   897	- Probe details (so you can explain failures quickly):
   898	  - `read` probe: the test writes a nonce file in the workspace and asks the agent to `read` it and echo the nonce back.
   899	  - `exec+read` probe: the test asks the agent to `exec`-write a nonce into a temp file, then `read` it back.
   900	  - image probe: the test attaches a generated PNG (cat + randomized code) and expects the model to return `cat <CODE>`.
   901	  - Implementation reference: `src/gateway/gateway-models.profiles.live.test.ts` and `test/helpers/live-image-probe.ts`.
   902	- How to enable:
   903	  - `pnpm test:live` (or `OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST=1` if invoking Vitest directly)
   904	- How to select models:
   905	  - Default: the curated high-signal (`modern`) priority list
   906	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_MODELS=small` runs the curated small-model list through the full gateway+agent pipeline
   907	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_MODELS=all` is an alias for `modern`
   908	  - Or set `OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_MODELS="provider/model"` (or comma list) to narrow
   909	  - Modern/all and small gateway sweeps default to their curated-list length as a cap; set `OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_MAX_MODELS=0` for an exhaustive selected sweep or a positive number for a smaller cap.
   910	- How to select providers (avoid "OpenRouter everything"):
   911	  - `OPENCLAW_LIVE_GATEWAY_PROVIDERS="google,google-gemini-cli,openai,anthropic,zai,minimax"` (comma allowlist)
   912	- Tool + image probes are always on in this live test:
   913	  - `read` probe + `exec+read` probe (tool stress)
   914	  - image probe runs when the model advertises image input support
   915	  - Flow (high level):
   916	    - Test generates a tiny PNG with "CAT" + random code (`test/helpers/live-image-probe.ts`)
   917	    - Sends it via `agent` `attachments: [{ mimeType: "image/png", content: "<base64>" }]`
   918	    - Gateway parses attachments into `images[]` (`src/gateway/server-methods/agent.ts` + `src/gateway/chat-attachments.ts`)
   919	    - Embedded agent forwards a multimodal user message to the model
   920	    - Assertion: reply contains `cat` + the code (OCR tolerance: minor mistakes allowed)
   921	
   922	<Tip>
   923	To see what you can test on your machine (and the exact `provider/model` ids), run:
   924	
   925	```bash
   926	openclaw models list
   927	openclaw models list --json
   928	```
   929	
   930	</Tip>
   931	---
   932	summary: "Ad hoc local media/voice smokes plus the Android node capability sweep"
   933	title: "Quick live smokes and the Android node sweep"
   934	read_when:
   935	  - You want a fast ad hoc media or voice-call live check
   936	  - You are sweeping the commands a connected Android node advertises
   937	---
   938	
   939	## Live: local smoke commands
   940	
   941	Export the needed provider key in the process environment before ad hoc live
   942	checks.
   943	
   944	Safe media smoke:
   945	
   946	```bash
   947	pnpm openclaw infer tts convert --local --json \
   948	  --text "OpenClaw live smoke." \
   949	  --output /tmp/openclaw-live-smoke.mp3
   950	```
   951	
   952	Safe voice-call readiness smoke:
   953	
   954	```bash
   955	pnpm openclaw voicecall setup --json
   956	pnpm openclaw voicecall smoke --to "+15555550123"
   957	```
   958	
   959	`voicecall smoke` is a dry run unless `--yes` is also present; use `--yes` only
   960	when you intend to place a real call. For Twilio, Telnyx, and Plivo, a
   961	successful readiness check requires a public webhook URL - local/private
   962	loopback URLs are rejected because those providers cannot reach them.
   963	
   964	## Live: Android node capability sweep
   965	
   966	- Test: `src/gateway/android-node.capabilities.live.test.ts`
   967	- Script: `pnpm android:test:integration`
   968	- Goal: invoke **every command currently advertised** by a connected Android node and assert command contract behavior.
   969	- Scope:
   970	  - Preconditioned/manual setup (the suite does not install/run/pair the app).
   971	  - Command-by-command gateway `node.invoke` validation for the selected Android node.
   972	- Required pre-setup:
   973	  - Android app already connected + paired to the gateway.
   974	  - App kept in foreground.
   975	  - Permissions/capture consent granted for capabilities you expect to pass.
   976	- Optional target overrides:
   977	  - `OPENCLAW_ANDROID_NODE_ID` or `OPENCLAW_ANDROID_NODE_NAME`.
   978	  - `OPENCLAW_ANDROID_GATEWAY_URL` / `OPENCLAW_ANDROID_GATEWAY_TOKEN` / `OPENCLAW_ANDROID_GATEWAY_PASSWORD`.
   979	- Full Android setup details: [Android App](/platforms/android)
   980	---
   981	summary: "Live (network-touching) tests: model matrix, CLI backends, ACP, media providers, credentials"
   982	read_when:
   983	  - Running live model matrix / CLI backend / ACP / media-provider smokes
   984	  - Debugging live-test credential resolution
   985	  - Adding a new provider-specific live test
   986	title: "Testing: live suites"
   987	sidebarTitle: "Live tests"
   988	---
   989	
   990	For quick start, QA runners, unit/integration suites, and Docker flows, see
   991	[Testing](/help/testing). This page covers **live** (network-touching) tests:
   992	model matrix, CLI backends, ACP, media providers, and credential handling.
   993	
   994	This page is an index. The live testing kit is documented on six pages, one
   995	per reader job. Open the page that matches your task.
   996	
   997	| Page                                                                                        | Read it when                                                                   |
   998	| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
   999	| [Quick live smokes and the Android node sweep](/help/testing-live/quick-smokes)             | You want a fast ad hoc smoke or an Android node sweep.                         |
  1000	| [Live model smoke (profile keys)](/help/testing-live/model-smoke)                           | You are smoking a provider or model through the direct and gateway layers.     |
  1001	| [CLI backend and APNs lanes](/help/testing-live/cli-backends)                               | You are driving a local CLI backend, or checking APNs proxy reachability.      |
  1002	| [ACP bind and Codex app-server lanes](/help/testing-live/acp-and-codex)                     | You are debugging an ACP bind or the Codex app-server harness.                 |
  1003	| [OpenAI long context and the live model matrix](/help/testing-live/long-context-and-matrix) | You need the long-context proof runs, the recipes, or the curated model lists. |
  1004	| [Media provider live lanes](/help/testing-live/media-providers)                             | You are running an image, music, video, or other media provider sweep.         |
  1005	
  1006	## Live tests vs your real gateway
  1007	
  1008	Live suites and ad hoc smokes must never disturb a gateway that is already
  1009	serving real traffic (yours or another operator's):
  1010	
  1011	- Bring your own gateway: use the in-process gateway (Layer 2 on
  1012	  [Live model smoke](/help/testing-live/model-smoke)) or start a
  1013	  dev instance with an isolated state dir (`OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR=<scratch>`) and a
  1014	  free port. Do not bind the default gateway port (18789) while a real gateway
  1015	  is running on it.
  1016	- Do not `openclaw gateway stop`/`restart` (or `launchctl`/`systemctl`/tmux
  1017	  equivalents) a service you did not start in this session — that is the
  1018	  operator's live instance. Get explicit approval first.
  1019	- Need realistic data? Copy the live state/DB into your dev state dir and test
  1020	  against the copy. In-place migrations of a live gateway's state also require
  1021	  explicit approval.
  1022	
  1023	## Credentials (never commit)
  1024	
  1025	Live tests discover credentials the same way the CLI does. Practical implications:
  1026	
  1027	- If the CLI works, live tests should find the same keys.
  1028	- If a live test says "no creds", debug the same way you'd debug `openclaw models list` / model selection.
  1029	- An OpenClaw live suite that cannot resolve its credentials must skip visibly in the reporter with Vitest test-context `skip(reason)` or fail; it must never pass green without reaching the provider, because a green run that did not reach the provider is not live evidence.
  1030	
  1031	- Per-agent auth profiles: SQLite credential rows in `~/.openclaw/agents/<agentId>/agent/openclaw-agent.sqlite` (this is what "profile keys" means in the live tests)
  1032	- Config: `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` (or `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH`)
  1033	- Legacy OAuth dir: `~/.openclaw/credentials/` (copied into the staged live home when present, but not the main profile-key store)
  1034	- Local live runs copy the active config (with `agents.*.workspace` / `agentDir` overrides stripped) and stage each agent's canonical SQLite auth credential/state rows through the auth-store reader/writer APIs, not by copying its database or the rest of its directory. Agent sessions, `workspace/`, and `sandboxes/` data are not staged. The runner also copies the legacy `credentials/` dir and supported external CLI auth files/dirs (`.claude.json`, `.claude/.credentials.json`, `.claude/settings*.json`, `.claude/backups`, `.codex/auth.json`, `.codex/config.toml`, `.gemini`, `.minimax`) into a temp test home.
  1035	
  1036	If you want to rely on env keys, export them before local tests or use the
  1037	Docker runners on the lane pages listed above with an explicit
  1038	`OPENCLAW_PROFILE_FILE`.
