    10	OpenClaw has three Vitest suites (unit/integration, e2e, live) plus Docker
    11	runners. This page covers what each suite covers, which command to run for a
    12	given workflow, how live tests discover credentials, and how to add
    13	regressions for real-world provider/model bugs.
    14	
    15	<Note>
    16	**QA stack (qa-lab, qa-channel, live transport lanes)** is documented separately:
    17	
    18	- [QA overview](/concepts/qa-e2e-automation) - architecture, command surface, scenario authoring, and the Matrix live lane.
    19	- [Maturity scorecard](/maturity/scorecard) - how release QA evidence supports stability and LTS decisions.
    20	- [QA channel](/channels/qa-channel) - the synthetic transport plugin used by repo-backed scenarios.
    21	
    22	This page covers the regular test suites and Docker/Parallels runners. [QA-specific runners](#qa-specific-runners) below lists the concrete `qa` invocations and points back at the references above.
