   621	### Anthropic runtime-context cache regression
   622	
   623	Run `pnpm test:docker:live-anthropic-cache` with `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` to verify
   624	the package-installed Anthropic provider and managed transport against
   625	`claude-sonnet-4-6`. The functional image uses the prepared candidate package;
   626	`OPENCLAW_SKIP_DOCKER_BUILD=1` reuses an existing image.
   627	First run `pnpm test:docker:live-anthropic-cache --mock` for secretless HTTP/SSE
   628	proof through the same installed builders. Mock output labels its synthetic
   629	usage; only the default live mode proves provider cache reads and writes.
   630	
   631	Each builder makes four requests: initial conversation, two actual tool-result
   632	continuations, and the next user turn. The harness moves a synthetic temporary
   633	runtime-context carrier to the request tail and checks that it never becomes a
   634	cache breakpoint or part of a cached prefix. The initial conversation must write
   635	at least 4,096 cache tokens; subsequent reads must reach 90% of that write and
   636	grow after each continuation, while new writes stay below 25% of the initial
   637	write. A short system prompt prevents a system-only cache hit from satisfying
   638	the conversation floor. Every request has a 90-second deadline and no retries.
   639	
   640	This blocking lane runs in the stable/full Full Release Validation Docker `core`
   641	chunk. Logs contain token usage and breakpoint positions, with synthetic prompt
   642	contents kept out of output. Gateway session lifecycle and retained runtime
   643	context remain covered by their owner tests.
   644	
