   782	profile includes profiler startup before the pagination timer begins. Compare
   783	repeated runs of the same fixture and build mode; keep the legacy test-driver
   784	wall timings separate from the browser timestamps.
   785	
   786	Successful and failed evidence is retained. Cleanup is manual: remove only exact
   787	directories that you own and have finished reviewing. Never recursively delete
   788	the shared parent before a replay. Disposable build/media fixtures and temporary
   789	raw video have their own cleanup. New captures cannot recover overwritten evidence;
   790	do not describe a replay as recovery of lost files.
   791	
   792	Timeout diagnostics allocate fresh children beneath the existing
   793	`OPENCLAW_UI_E2E_DIAGNOSTIC_DIR` or default timeout directory. Each child keeps its
   794	raw `failure.private.json` report and captured `failure.private.png` screenshot
   795	local, alongside an allowlisted `failure.public.json` summary. Automatic CI uploads
   796	match only `failure-*/failure.public.json`; raw reports and screenshots remain
   797	private. Older frozen targets without the public summary produce no matching
   798	upload and never fall back to raw captures.
   799	
   800	The shared suite captures native test timeouts before draining routes and closing
   801	the owned browser context. Cleanup and the pending test body join the same capture,
   802	so a later closed-page error does not replace the original timeout evidence.
   803	
   804	The shared failure collector gives renderer evaluation and screenshot capture one
   805	five-second budget. If the renderer stalls, it records incomplete diagnostics and
   806	returns so the caller can rethrow the original failure. A late browser response
   807	cannot publish a screenshot after that budget expires; test action deadlines and
   808	caller-owned browser cleanup remain unchanged.
   809	
   810	The private JSON report's `ci.shardIndex` and `ci.vitestShardCount` fields record
   811	`VITEST_SHARD_INDEX` and `VITEST_SHARD_COUNT`, respectively, as supplied by normal CI.
   812	Missing values remain `null`; manual and separate release E2E invocations do not
   813	infer this metadata from Vitest's `--shard` argument.
   814	
   815	Mantis allocates an invocation directory for setup logs,
   816	capture attempts, and its report; the builder preserves each attempt's relative
   817	paths and refuses to overwrite an existing report.
   818	
   819	Separate output owners remain, including `chat-attachment-read-lifecycle`.
   820	Do not assume unmigrated owners share this retention guarantee.
   821	
   822	### Screenshots during Chromium recordings
   823	
   824	The session-host command-state real-Gateway proof uses `page.screenshot({ path })`
   825	without `clip` or `fullPage: true`, keeping its existing viewport, recording size,
   826	waits, and animation options. This path was verified on Linux with Playwright
   827	1.62.1 and full Chrome for Testing 151.0.7922.34.
   828	
   829	Other recording owners have not been migrated or certified by this proof; some
   830	still use locator or full-page screenshots. This is not a suite-wide capture
   831	policy. Verify each owner's screenshot content and finalized video before
   832	changing its capture mode. When using the verified viewport path, crop any
   833	element-only PNG outside the browser. Cropping cannot recover missing content
   834	from an already-corrupted recording.
   835	
   836	In a macOS arm64 reproduction with Playwright 1.62.1 and its bundled full Chrome
   837	for Testing 151.0.7922.34, `locator.screenshot()` and
   838	`page.screenshot({ clip })` caused small screencast frames. The element appears at
   839	the video origin with gray elsewhere, even though the PNG, DOM geometry, and
   840	functional assertions are correct. `fullPage: true` is not a general workaround:
   841	a document larger than the viewport can instead produce a shrunken page with
   842	gray padding. Unclipped viewport captures preserved the recording in the same
   843	synthetic reproduction; other browser versions and platforms require their own
   844	verification.
   845	
   846	This is an upstream capture limitation, not a Gateway or context-cleanup failure.
   847	[Chromium's screenshot handler](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/151.0.7922.34/content/browser/devtools/protocol/page_handler.cc#1492)
   848	temporarily changes the shared view size and restores it after capture; its
   849	screencast producer can observe the intermediate surface.
   850	[Playwright's recorder](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/v1.62.1/packages/playwright-core/src/server/videoRecorder.ts#L166)
   851	pads undersized frames with gray. Closing the context finalizes the video but
   852	does not repair those frames. Do not filter out bad frames or change UI behavior
   853	to conceal this limitation.
   854	
   855	Verify finalized video content around every capture, not just its dimensions or
   856	the success of locator assertions. For a dependency upgrade, reproduce with a
   857	synthetic page containing an offset small element, compare element, clipped,
   858	viewport, and oversized full-page screenshots, and inspect every decoded frame.
   859	Keep real host/profile footage local; inspect public proof for synthetic-only
   860	content before sharing. Correct PNGs remain useful still-image proof, but a
   861	corrupted video is not continuous-flow proof.
   862	
   863	## Gateway and E2E
   864	
   865	- Gateway tests are included in the untargeted `pnpm test` full suite; run them alone with `pnpm test:gateway`.
   866	- `pnpm test:e2e`: repo E2E aggregate = `pnpm test:e2e:gateway && pnpm test:e2e:agent-plugin-gateway && pnpm test:ui:e2e`.
   867	- `pnpm test:e2e:gateway`: gateway end-to-end smoke tests (multi-instance WS/HTTP/node pairing). Defaults to `threads` + `isolate: false` with one worker in `vitest.e2e.config.ts`; opt into parallelism with `OPENCLAW_E2E_WORKERS=<n>` (capped at 16), and enable verbose logs with `OPENCLAW_E2E_VERBOSE=1`.
   868	  Broad runs prepare the shared runtime once, then use four sequential Vitest shards in fresh processes to bound worker memory. The worker limit applies within each process; ordinary test failures are retained while remaining shards finish. Explicit filters, watch mode, caller-supplied shards, coverage, and report-output options keep one direct invocation.
   869	- `pnpm test:live`: provider live tests (Claude/Minimax/DeepSeek/z.ai/etc, gated by `*.live.test.ts`). Requires API keys and `LIVE=1` (or `OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST=1`) to unskip; verbose output with `OPENCLAW_LIVE_TEST_QUIET=0`.
