   640	summary: "Recovering from a rejected config and reading gateway probe warnings"
   641	title: "Config validation and probes"
   642	sidebarTitle: "Config validation and probes"
   643	read_when:
   644	  - The Gateway rejected an invalid config and you need the recovery path
   645	  - You need to know what the `.rejected`, `.bak`, and last-known-good copies hold
   646	  - Gateway probe warnings appear in status or doctor output
   647	---
   648	
   649	## Gateway rejected invalid config
   650	
   651	Use when Gateway startup fails with `Invalid config` or hot reload logs say it skipped an invalid edit.
   652	
   653	Startup automatically migrates deterministic legacy keys in eligible single-file
   654	configs and continues only if the entire result validates, including plugins. It
   655	keeps the previous config in the `.bak` ring. Configs using `$include`, Nix-managed
   656	configs, configs written by a newer version, and configs that still fail validation
   657	require operator repair. See [Legacy config key migrations](/gateway/doctor#detailed-behavior-and-rationale).
   658	
   659	```bash
   660	openclaw logs --follow
   661	openclaw config file
   662	openclaw config validate
   663	openclaw doctor
   664	```
   665	
   666	Look for:
   667	
   668	- `Invalid config at ...`
   669	- `config reload skipped (invalid config): ...`
   670	- `Config write rejected: ...`
   671	- A timestamped `openclaw.json.rejected.*` file beside the active config.
   672	- A timestamped `openclaw.json.clobbered.*` file if `doctor --fix` repaired a broken direct edit.
   673	- OpenClaw keeps the latest 32 `.clobbered.*` files for each config path and rotates older ones.
   674	
   675	<AccordionGroup>
   676	  <Accordion title="What happened">
   677	    - The config did not validate during startup, hot reload, or an OpenClaw-owned write.
   678	    - Gateway startup leaves `openclaw.json` unchanged and fails closed when safe legacy-key migration cannot produce a fully valid config.
   679	    - Hot reload skips invalid external edits and keeps the current runtime config active.
   680	    - OpenClaw-owned writes reject invalid/destructive payloads before commit and save `.rejected.*`.
   681	    - `openclaw doctor --fix` owns repairs beyond automatic legacy-key migration. It can remove non-JSON prefixes or restore the last-known-good copy while preserving the rejected payload as `.clobbered.*`.
   682	    - When many repairs happen for one config path, OpenClaw rotates older `.clobbered.*` files so the newest repaired payload is still available.
   683	
   684	  </Accordion>
   685	  <Accordion title="Inspect and repair">
   686	    ```bash
   687	    CONFIG="$(openclaw config file)"
   688	    ls -lt "$CONFIG".clobbered.* "$CONFIG".rejected.* 2>/dev/null | head
   689	    diff -u "$CONFIG" "$(ls -t "$CONFIG".clobbered.* 2>/dev/null | head -n 1)"
   690	    openclaw config validate
   691	    openclaw doctor
   692	    ```
   693	  </Accordion>
   694	  <Accordion title="Common signatures">
   695	    - `.clobbered.*` exists → doctor preserved a broken external edit while repairing the active config.
   696	    - `.rejected.*` exists → an OpenClaw-owned config write failed schema or clobber checks before commit.
   697	    - `Config write rejected:` → the write tried to drop required shape, shrink the file sharply, or persist invalid config.
   698	    - `config reload skipped (invalid config):` → a direct edit failed validation and was ignored by the running Gateway.
   699	    - `Invalid config at ...` → startup failed before Gateway services booted.
   700	    - `missing-meta-vs-last-good`, `gateway-mode-missing-vs-last-good`, or `size-drop-vs-last-good:*` → an OpenClaw-owned write was rejected because it lost fields or size compared with the last-known-good backup.
   701	    - `Config last-known-good promotion skipped` → the candidate contained redacted secret placeholders such as `***`.
   702	
   703	  </Accordion>
   704	  <Accordion title="Fix options">
   705	    An interactive startup can offer to run `openclaw doctor --fix` and retry once when automatic legacy-key migration is not enough. Non-interactive startup prints the repair command instead.
   706	
   707	    1. Run `openclaw doctor --fix` to let doctor repair prefixed/clobbered config or restore last-known-good.
   708	    2. Copy only the intended keys from `.clobbered.*` or `.rejected.*`, then apply them with `openclaw config set` or `config.patch`.
   709	    3. Run `openclaw config validate` before restarting.
   710	    4. If you edit by hand, keep the full JSON5 config, not just the partial object you wanted to change.
   711	
   712	  </Accordion>
   713	</AccordionGroup>
   714	
   715	Related:
   716	
   717	- [Config](/cli/config)
   718	- [Configuration: hot reload](/gateway/configuration#config-hot-reload)
   719	- [Configuration: strict validation](/gateway/configuration#strict-validation)
   720	- [Doctor](/gateway/doctor)
   721	
   722	## Gateway probe warnings
   723	
   724	Use when `openclaw gateway probe` reaches something, but still prints a warning block.
   725	
   726	```bash
   727	openclaw gateway probe
   728	openclaw gateway probe --json
   729	openclaw gateway probe --ssh user@gateway-host
   730	```
   731	
   732	Look for:
   733	
   734	- `warnings[].code` and `primaryTargetId` in JSON output.
   735	- Whether the warning is about SSH fallback, multiple gateways, missing scopes, or unresolved auth refs.
   736	
   737	Common signatures:
   738	
   739	- `SSH tunnel failed to start; falling back to direct probes.` → SSH setup failed, but the command still tried direct configured/loopback targets.
   740	- `multiple reachable gateway identities detected` → distinct gateways answered, or OpenClaw could not prove reachable targets are the same gateway. An SSH tunnel, proxy URL, or configured remote URL to the same gateway is treated as one gateway with multiple transports, even when transport ports differ.
   741	- `Read-probe diagnostics are limited by gateway scopes (missing operator.read)` → connect worked, but detail RPC is scope-limited; pair device identity or use credentials with `operator.read`.
   742	- `Gateway accepted the WebSocket connection, but follow-up read diagnostics failed` → connect worked, but the full diagnostic RPC set timed out or failed. Treat this as a reachable Gateway with degraded diagnostics; compare `connect.ok` and `connect.rpcOk` in `--json` output.
   743	- `Capability: pairing-pending` or `gateway closed (1008): pairing required` → the gateway answered, but this client still needs pairing/approval before normal operator access.
   744	- Unresolved `gateway.auth.*` / `gateway.remote.*` SecretRef warning text → auth material was unavailable in this command path for the failed target.
   745	
   746	Related:
   747	
   748	- [Gateway](/cli/gateway)
   749	- [Multiple gateways on the same host](/gateway#multiple-gateways-same-host)
   750	- [Remote access](/gateway/remote)
